      ],
      "pins": [
        "R5.1",
        "R5.2",
        "U2.6",
        "U3.6",
        "J4.1"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "VCC",
        "PWM",
        "+5V"
      ],
      "observed": "R5 is a 1 kΩ pull-up connected between the unregulated VCC rail and the PWM net. The PWM net is also connected directly to ATtiny I/O pins U2.6/U3.6 and to the AVR-ISP MISO pin J4.1, without any clamp on that net.",
      "expected": "A pull-up on an ATtiny logic/ISP signal should reference the regulated MCU supply (+5V), not the regulator input VCC. The netlist shows VCC feeding LM1117-5.0 to produce +5V, implying VCC is the higher fan/power input rail; pulling MCU pins to that rail is not sound design practice.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "R5 | 1K | Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric | Device:R_Small | Resistor, small symbol"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "VCC : C1.1(passive) J2.4(Pin_4,passive) J5.2(Pin_2,passive) JP1.2(B,passive) Q1.2(S,passive) R1.1(passive) R5.1(passive) R6.1(passive) U1.3(VI,power_in)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "PWM : J4.1(MISO,passive) R2.1(passive) R5.2(passive) U2.6(PB1,bidirectional) U3.6(PB1,bidirectional)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U1 | LM1117-5.0 | Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-223-3_TabPin2 | fan_controller-rescue:LM1117-5.0-Regulator_Linear"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "+5V : C2.1(passive) J3.1(Pin_1,passive) J4.2(VCC,passive) J6.2(Pin_2,passive) R3.1(passive) U1.2(VO,power_out) U2.8(VCC,power_in) U3.8(VCC,power_in)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If VCC is the regulator input and therefore higher than +5V, the PWM node can be pulled above the MCU supply, overstressing U2.6/U3.6 and the ISP MISO line. This can cause latch-up, damage, or incorrect fan-drive behavior. If VCC were already 5V, the LM1117-5.0 rail separation would itself be inconsistent.",
      "confidence": 0.65
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The PWM pull-up R5 is tied to the unregulated VCC rail while the PWM net connects directly to ATtiny and ISP pins; with the LM1117-5.0 architecture this is inconsistent with standard logic-level pull-up practice and can overvoltage the MCU/programmer pins."
}

